# Code owners for go-service-kit.
#
# This module is imported by every Rebuy Go service, so a change here ships to all
# of them at once. Owners are the people who actually write Go here — named
# individuals rather than a team, deliberately: the Go contributor set does not map
# onto any existing GitHub team, and pointing at `devops` would route reviews to
# people who do not work in this language.
#
# ── What this file does, and what it does not ────────────────────────────────
#
# It AUTO-REQUESTS review from the owners on every PR. It does NOT block merge:
# `main` runs the standard protection tier — 1 approval, `devops` in
# `pull_request_bypassers`, no push restriction — set in the github-rbac stack in
# shared-infrastructure.
#
# That combination is deliberate (Jared, 2026-08-19). Enforcing owner review means
# `require_code_owner_reviews = true`, which in that module only exists on the
# STRICT tier — and the strict tier also restricts pushes to the `devops` team.
# Under a push restriction, write-role users cannot merge their own PRs (measured
# org-wide closing DO-388; `senator-rebuy` hit exactly this on admin-nextjs #53).
# Four of the five owners below are not in `devops`, so enforcing owner review via
# that tier would lock the owners out of merging the code they own.
#
# If enforcement is wanted later, the fix is a per-repo `require_code_owner_reviews`
# override on the standard tier, not a move to strict.
#
# ── Roster ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A starting point, not a closed list — the main Go contributors as of 2026-08-19.
# Add people as the Go footprint grows. Removing someone is the part that needs
# care: an owner who leaves and is not removed leaves a review request nobody
# answers.

